      "extract": "Richard Feynman described electron diffraction as a phenomenon \"which has in it the heart of quantum mechanics. In reality, it contains the *only* mystery\"[@Feynman65]. He went on to describe a thought experiment for which he stated \"that you should not try to set up\" because \"the apparatus would have to be made on an impossibly small scale to show the effects we are interested in.\" He used these effects to help",
